@h1 Skill: claude-api (AGD-decomposed) [#h-root]

@h2 Router [#h-router]

@x-reference desc="entry point: routing map for claude-api skill" refs="#claude-api-defaults,#claude-api-output-rule,#claude-api-provider-check,#claude-api-lang-detect,#claude-api-task-router" [#claude-api-skill]
~~~
TRIGGERS: code imports `anthropic` / `@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for Claude API,
Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature
(caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model.
SKIP: file imports `openai` / other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`.

ALWAYS-RUN gates (apply on every task):
  #claude-api-provider-check   pre-flight: detect non-Anthropic markers, refuse if mismatch
  #claude-api-output-rule      SDK-vs-raw-HTTP rule
  #claude-api-defaults         model + thinking + streaming defaults

NAVIGATION:
  Detect language          → #claude-api-lang-detect (then #ref-claude-api-{lang})
  Pick a surface/tier      → #claude-api-surface-table → #claude-api-decision-tree
  Per-task routing         → #claude-api-task-router (translates user intent → file fetches)
  Lookup tables            → #claude-api-models-current, #claude-api-thinking-table,
                             #claude-api-caching-quick, #claude-api-compaction-quick,
                             #claude-api-lang-features
  Managed Agents           → #claude-api-managed-agents
  Architecture decisions   → #claude-api-architecture
  Pitfalls (tagged)        → fetch the matching #claude-api-pitfall-* with the relevant feature

WebFetch live docs only when: user says "latest"/"current", cached data looks wrong,
or feature isn't covered. URLs in shared/live-sources.md.
~~~

@h2 Always-run gates [#h-gates]

@x-reference desc="pre-flight: detect non-Anthropic providers, refuse on mismatch" [#claude-api-provider-check]
~~~
Scan target file (or prompt + project) for non-Anthropic markers:
  `import openai` · `from openai` · `langchain_openai` · `OpenAI(`
  `gpt-4` · `gpt-5` · file names like `agent-openai.py` · `*-generic.py`
  any explicit instruction to keep code provider-neutral

If found: STOP. Tell user this skill produces Claude/Anthropic SDK code; ask whether
they want to switch the file to Claude or want a non-Claude implementation.
Do NOT edit a non-Anthropic file with Anthropic SDK calls.
~~~

@x-reference desc="output rule: SDK vs raw HTTP, never mix, no OpenAI shims" [#claude-api-output-rule]
~~~
When user asks to add/modify/implement a Claude feature, code MUST call Claude through ONE of:

1. Official Anthropic SDK for the project's language
   (`anthropic`, `@anthropic-ai/sdk`, `com.anthropic.*`, etc.)
   DEFAULT whenever a supported SDK exists.

2. Raw HTTP (`curl`, `requests`, `fetch`, `httpx`)
   ONLY when user explicitly asks for cURL/REST/raw HTTP, project is shell/cURL,
   or language has no official SDK.

NEVER mix the two. NEVER use OpenAI-compatible shims.

NEVER guess SDK usage. Function/class names, namespaces, signatures, import paths
must come from explicit docs — `{lang}/` files in skill, official SDK repos, or
shared/live-sources.md. If a binding isn't documented, WebFetch the SDK repo
BEFORE writing code. Do not infer Ruby/Java/Go/PHP/C# APIs from cURL or other lang.
~~~

@x-reference desc="defaults: Opus 4.7 + adaptive thinking + streaming-when-long" refs="#claude-api-models-current,#claude-api-thinking-table,#claude-api-pitfall-thinking-47,#claude-api-pitfall-max-tokens" [#claude-api-defaults]
~~~
Unless user requests otherwise:

MODEL    : Claude Opus 4.7 — model string `claude-opus-4-7`
THINKING : adaptive — `thinking: {type: "adaptive"}` for anything remotely complex
STREAMING: any request with long input, long output, or high `max_tokens` — prevents
           hitting request timeouts. Use SDK `.get_final_message()` / `.finalMessage()`
           helper to get the complete response if you don't need individual stream events.

Other models / older patterns → see #claude-api-models-current
Thinking config per model     → see #claude-api-thinking-table
Common max_tokens trap        → see #claude-api-pitfall-max-tokens
~~~

@h2 Lookup tables [#h-lookups]

@x-reference desc="file-extension → language → folder lookup" refs="#claude-api-lang-features,#ref-claude-api-python,#ref-claude-api-typescript,#ref-claude-api-java,#ref-claude-api-go,#ref-claude-api-ruby,#ref-claude-api-csharp,#ref-claude-api-php,#ref-claude-api-curl" [#claude-api-lang-detect]
~~~
1. Infer from project files:

  *.py, requirements.txt, pyproject.toml, setup.py, Pipfile      → Python   → python/
  *.ts, *.tsx, package.json, tsconfig.json                       → TypeScript → typescript/
  *.js, *.jsx (no .ts files)                                     → TypeScript (JS uses same SDK)
  *.java, pom.xml, build.gradle                                  → Java     → java/
  *.kt, *.kts, build.gradle.kts                                  → Java (Kotlin uses Java SDK)
  *.scala, build.sbt                                             → Java (Scala uses Java SDK)
  *.go, go.mod                                                   → Go       → go/
  *.rb, Gemfile                                                  → Ruby     → ruby/
  *.cs, *.csproj                                                 → C#       → csharp/
  *.php, composer.json                                           → PHP      → php/

2. Multiple langs detected → check current file or ask:
   "I detected both X and Y. Which language are you using?"

3. Can't infer → AskUserQuestion (Python/TypeScript/Java/Go/Ruby/cURL/C#/PHP).
   If unavailable, default Python and note it.

4. Unsupported lang (Rust/Swift/C++/Elixir) → suggest cURL from curl/, mention
   community SDKs may exist, offer Python/TS as reference.

5. User asks for cURL/raw HTTP → curl/.
~~~

