~~~
| Language   | Tool Runner | Managed Agents | Notes                                 |
|------------|-------------|----------------|---------------------------------------|
| Python     | Yes (beta)  | Yes (beta)     | Full — `@beta_tool` decorator         |
| TypeScript | Yes (beta)  | Yes (beta)     | Full — `betaZodTool` + Zod            |
| Java       | Yes (beta)  | Yes (beta)     | Beta tool use with annotated classes  |
| Go         | Yes (beta)  | Yes (beta)     | `BetaToolRunner` in `toolrunner` pkg  |
| Ruby       | Yes (beta)  | Yes (beta)     | `BaseTool` + `tool_runner` in beta    |
| C#         | No          | No             | Official SDK only                     |
| PHP        | Yes (beta)  | Yes (beta)     | `BetaRunnableTool` + `toolRunner()`   |
| cURL       | N/A         | Yes (beta)     | Raw HTTP, no SDK features             |
~~~

@x-reference desc="use-case → tier → recommended surface" refs="#claude-api-decision-tree,#claude-api-architecture" [#claude-api-surface-table]
~~~
START SIMPLE. Default to simplest tier that meets needs. Single API calls handle most
cases — only reach for agents when task genuinely requires open-ended exploration.

| Use case                                          | Tier            | Surface                   |
|---------------------------------------------------|-----------------|---------------------------|
| Classification, summarization, extraction, Q&A    | Single LLM call | Claude API                |
| Batch processing or embeddings                    | Single LLM call | Claude API (batch endpt)  |
| Multi-step pipeline w/ code-controlled logic      | Workflow        | Claude API + tool use     |
| Open-ended task w/ unknown # of steps             | Agent           | Tool runner / Managed Ag. |
| Persistent agents w/ workspace, sessions          | Managed Agent   | Anthropic Managed Agents  |

For "should I build an agent?" → #claude-api-decision-tree
For deeper architecture choices → #claude-api-architecture
~~~

@x-reference desc="agent-vs-workflow decision tree" [#claude-api-decision-tree]
~~~
Build an AGENT only when ALL of:
- Task has no fixed steps (open-ended exploration)
- Number of steps is unknown ahead of time
- Branching depends on prior tool results
- Outcome quality justifies extra latency + cost

Otherwise prefer WORKFLOW (you write the loop in code) — predictable, debuggable,
cheaper, faster. Most "agent" requests are actually workflows in disguise.
~~~

@x-reference desc="architecture: bash-vs-dedicated tools, context mgmt, caching strategy" [#claude-api-architecture]
~~~
Concept-only summary. For depth: shared/agent-design.md.

Tool surface:
  bash tool        — flexible, agent-driven; wide attack surface
  dedicated tools  — typed, narrow, easier to validate; more upfront design

Context management (3 mechanisms, pick by lifetime):
  context editing  — drop old turns mid-conversation (transient)
  compaction       — summarize when nearing window (medium)
  memory tool      — persistent across sessions (long-lived)

Caching: design for prefix stability (system prompts + tool defs first).
See #claude-api-caching-quick and shared/prompt-caching.md.
~~~

@x-reference desc="current Claude models + strings (cached: 2026-04-15)" refs="#ref-claude-api-shared-live-sources" [#claude-api-models-current]
~~~
Cached snapshot — re-fetch shared/live-sources.md if user asks for "latest".

  Family   | String                        | Notes
  ---------+-------------------------------+----------------------------------------
  Opus 4.7 | claude-opus-4-7               | Default. Adaptive thinking only.
           |                               | budget_tokens / temperature / top_p / top_k
           |                               | all REMOVED. Prefills return 400.
  Opus 4.6 | claude-opus-4-6               | Adaptive thinking. Prefills return 400.
