@x-reference desc="thinking config per model (quick reference)" refs="#claude-api-pitfall-thinking-47" [#claude-api-thinking-table]
~~~
| Model        | Config                                  | Notes                       |
|--------------|-----------------------------------------|-----------------------------|
| Opus 4.7     | thinking: {type: "adaptive"}            | ONLY adaptive. budget=400.  |
| Opus 4.6     | thinking: {type: "adaptive"}            | budget_tokens deprecated    |
| Sonnet 4.6   | thinking: {type: "adaptive"}            | budget_tokens deprecated    |
| Older models | thinking: {type:"enabled", budget_tokens:N} | budget < max_tokens, ≥1024 |

For migration of existing budget_tokens code → shared/model-migration.md
(transitional escape hatch; does NOT apply to Opus 4.7).
~~~

@x-reference desc="prompt caching — quick reference" refs="#ref-claude-api-shared-prompt-caching" [#claude-api-caching-quick]
~~~
Apps built with this skill SHOULD include prompt caching.

Principles (full doc: shared/prompt-caching.md → #ref-claude-api-shared-prompt-caching):
- Design for PREFIX STABILITY: put system prompts + tool defs FIRST and don't mutate them
- Place cache_control breakpoints at stable boundaries (end of system, end of tools)
- DO NOT interleave volatile content (timestamps, request IDs) into cached prefixes
- Anti-pattern: appending dynamic context to system prompt (silently invalidates)

If user asks "why is my cache hit rate low" → fetch shared/prompt-caching.md.
~~~

@x-reference desc="compaction — quick reference (long conversations)" [#claude-api-compaction-quick]
~~~
For long-running conversations that may exceed the context window, use COMPACTION:
the SDK's built-in helper summarizes older turns when usage approaches the limit.

For detail (when to compact, what's preserved, interaction with tools):
read {lang}/claude-api/README.md → Compaction section.

Alternative mechanisms (lifetime trade-off):
  context editing  → transient drops
  memory tool      → persistent across sessions
~~~

