@h2 Managed Agents [#h-managed-agents]

@x-reference desc="Managed Agents (Beta) — overview + critical lifecycle rule" refs="#ref-claude-api-managed-agents-overview,#ref-claude-api-shared-managed-agents-client-patterns" [#claude-api-managed-agents]
~~~
Managed Agents = server-managed stateful agents with workspace.

CRITICAL: Agents are PERSISTENT. Create ONCE, reference by ID.
  - Store the agent ID returned by `agents.create`
  - Pass it to every subsequent `sessions.create`
  - DO NOT call `agents.create` in the request path

Per-language READMEs: Python/TypeScript/Go/Ruby/PHP/Java/cURL → {lang}/managed-agents/README.md
Concept files (language-agnostic): shared/managed-agents-*.md

Anthropic CLI = convenient way to create agents/environments from version-controlled YAML
(URL in shared/live-sources.md).

Client code patterns (stream reconnect, processed_at gate, interrupt, tool_confirmation,
idle/terminated break, post-idle status race, file-mount gotchas, host-side credentials):
→ shared/managed-agents-client-patterns.md

C# does NOT support Managed Agents — use raw HTTP from curl/managed-agents.md.
~~~

@h2 Pitfalls (tagged per-feature, fetched with the feature) [#h-pitfalls]

@x-reference desc="pitfall: Opus 4.7 thinking is adaptive-only, budget_tokens returns 400" [#claude-api-pitfall-thinking-47]
~~~
Opus 4.7: thinking: {type: "enabled", budget_tokens: N} returns 400.
budget_tokens fully REMOVED on Opus 4.7 (along with temperature, top_p, top_k).
Use thinking: {type: "adaptive"}.
~~~

@x-reference desc="pitfall: 4.6/4.7 family removed assistant prefills (400 error)" [#claude-api-pitfall-prefill-removed]
~~~
Assistant message prefills (last-assistant-turn prefills) return 400 on:
  Opus 4.6, Opus 4.7, Sonnet 4.6.

Use structured outputs (output_config.format) or system prompt instructions to control
response format instead.
~~~

@x-reference desc="pitfall: max_tokens defaults — don't lowball, watch streaming threshold" [#claude-api-pitfall-max-tokens]
~~~
Don't lowball max_tokens — hitting cap truncates output mid-thought, requires retry.

Defaults:
  non-streaming requests: ~16000   (keeps under SDK HTTP timeouts)
  streaming requests:     ~64000   (timeouts not a concern, give the model room)
  classification only:    ~256
  cost caps / deliberately short: lower

128K output (Opus 4.6 + 4.7): SDKs require streaming for values that large to avoid
HTTP timeouts. Use .stream() with .get_final_message() / .finalMessage().
~~~

@x-reference desc="pitfall: tool call JSON parsing — always parse, never string-match" [#claude-api-pitfall-tool-json-parsing]
~~~
Opus 4.6, Opus 4.7, Sonnet 4.6 may produce different JSON string escaping in tool call
`input` fields (Unicode or forward-slash escaping).

Always parse tool inputs with json.loads() / JSON.parse() — never raw-string-match
the serialized input.
~~~

@x-reference desc="pitfall: confirm migration scope before editing files" [#claude-api-pitfall-migration-scope]
~~~
When user asks to migrate code to a newer Claude model WITHOUT naming a specific
file/dir/list, ASK which scope to apply first. Do not start editing until confirmed.

Imperative phrasings still ambiguous: "migrate my codebase", "move my project to X",
"upgrade to Sonnet 4.6", bare "migrate to Opus 4.7" — they say WHAT, not WHERE.

Proceed without asking ONLY when prompt names: exact file ("migrate `app.py`"),
specific dir ("under `services/`"), or explicit list ("update `a.py` and `b.py`").

Reference: shared/model-migration.md Step 0.
~~~

@x-reference desc="pitfall: don't truncate inputs silently" [#claude-api-pitfall-no-truncate]
~~~
Don't truncate inputs when passing files/content to the API.
If content is too long for context window, NOTIFY user and discuss options
(chunking, summarization, etc.) rather than silently truncating.
~~~

@x-reference desc="pitfall: don't reimplement SDK helpers; don't redefine SDK types" [#claude-api-pitfall-no-reimpl-sdk]
~~~
SDK provides high-level helpers — use them, don't rebuild.
  Use stream.finalMessage()  not  wrapping .on() events in new Promise()
  Use typed exception classes (Anthropic.RateLimitError, etc.)  not  string-matching errors
  Use SDK types (Anthropic.MessageParam, Anthropic.Tool, Anthropic.Message)
    not redefining equivalent interfaces

Defining your own `interface ChatMessage { role: string; content: unknown }` duplicates
what the SDK provides and loses type safety.

Structured outputs: use output_config: {format: {...}} — the deprecated `output_format`
parameter is gone. (General API change, not 4.6-specific.)
~~~

